  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Current behavior is to check the journal file with the earliest timestamp - if that has the wrong repository hash, complain and give up.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "New behavior would be the same check, and the same complaint on wrong repository hash, but don't give up, continue polling as before. That way, if the journal files merely arrived in the wrong sequence, the recovery would continue when the correct file arrived.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "This use case applies when the journal files are being copied in bulk from one location to another. Currently, it is necessary to stop the follower while moving the files, in order to prevent this scenario.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
